Z||000023||bHooper||06-26-2001||10:12 AM||||you ask about lowering the cradle<P>here go's:<BR>1) you will need need an 8' 4x4, preferably 2 floor jacks (but you can get by with one), one pair of jack stands and some scrap pieces' of 2x4 or blocks.<P>2) b4 tilting the engine, remove the heat shield and pipes from the v-6 cooling fan.  also, disconnect the two grounding straps, and the air intake.  if you don't do this, the shields will catch on the manifold<BR>and be difficult to move.  you can also opt to remove the dog bone (for more travel). i prefer to do it at the trunk mount, so that i have something to work with when putting the car back together.<P>3) place the 4x4 under the car, just in front of the cradle and directly under the coolant tube brackets (this is very important), prop it up, on each end, so that you can get your jack/s under it.<P>4) place your jack under the rear of the cradle, just enough to lift it a bit.  using a 15 mm socket, remove the two rear cradle bolts.  once these are out, you can lower the rear of the car.  the engine and cradle<BR>should be tilting a bit.<P>5) jack up one side of the car, blocking it (unless you have two jacks) and then do the other side. eventually, you will reach a point that you may decide to remove the nuts that attach the strut's to the car, that is ok.<P>6) reassembly is the reverse.<P>good luck!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
